  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "E2E WAL Read / Consume — read from top to bottom",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Memory or historical WAL → SN Scanner → subscription → processing / visibility**\n\nSelect a time window containing the workload. Channel filters apply to Milvus channel metrics; log filters apply to WP metrics. They are independent identities: use wpcli metadata to map them; there is no automatic channel-to-log or collection-to-log join. Legends identify the actual process.\n\n**No data ≠ healthy zero.** Lazy/error/remote-only metrics may be absent; `./stack.sh verify` records each stage's coverage. Timers overlap and quantiles are not additive. Read each step's guidance before interpreting an idle signal."
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "1. Establish the read mode — memory tailing or WAL catchup",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to use this step",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "A tailing scanner can read the SN write-ahead memory buffer without WP RPCs. A cold/catchup reader may read an active segment from WP services or a compacted segment directly from object storage. Zero WP read traffic alone is not a fault. EOF/end_of_file is normal at the tail. Compare scanner modes and WP read sources before interpreting an idle backend. For a true durability test, use a separate controlled restart/recovery scenario."
      },
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scanners by mode",
      "description": "",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "range": true,
          "expr": "sum by (pod,channel_name,scanner_model) (milvus_wal_scanner_total{cluster=\"$cluster\",namespace=\"$namespace\",woodpecker_id=\"$woodpecker_id\",component=\"streamingnode\",channel_name=~\"${channel:regex}\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{channel_name}} {{scanner_model}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 5,
            "spanNulls": false,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 4,
